    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Workday is a publicly traded enterprise software company, founded in 2005 and headquartered in Pleasanton, CA, that provides cloud-based applications for human resources, finance, and IT. The company trades on the stock exchange under the ticker WDAY and reported revenue of $9,552,000,000 for the fiscal year ending January 31, 2026, according to its most recent 10-K filing.\n\nThe company describes its platform as an enterprise AI system spanning HR, finance, and IT, with its core AI product tracked as Workday AI. The site highlights agentic AI capabilities developed with Sana, describing specialized agents that can, in its framing, find, build, act, and automate across key business processes. Workday AI is also noted for skills-based talent management, predictive analytics, and handling sensitive HR data.\n\nWorkday faces a notable volume of federal litigation. Cases on record include multiple actions by Meckfessel Poletti in the Eastern District of California, Williams v. Workday in the Northern District of Georgia, Elias v. Workday in the Northern District of California, Noriega and Doe proceedings in the District of Colorado, and Hill v. Workday filed in both the District of Maryland and the Eastern District of Virginia.",
